  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Definite integrals measure areas between curves, volumes of solids, and average values.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Area, volume, average",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Area between curves: \\( \\displaystyle\\int(\\text{top}-\\text{bottom})\\,dx \\). Volumes by <strong>disks/washers</strong> about an axis. Average value: \\( \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f \\). Solids with known cross-sections integrate the section area.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int(\\text{top}-\\text{bot}) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Disk",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\pi\\displaystyle\\int R^{2}\\,dx \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Washer",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\pi\\displaystyle\\int (R^{2}-r^{2}) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Average value",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\displaystyle\\int_a^b f \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area between \\( y=x \\) and \\( y=x^{2} \\) on \\( [0,1] \\).</p>\\[ \\int_0^1\\big(x-x^{2}\\big)\\,dx=\\frac12-\\frac13=\\frac16. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Disk/washer volume",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the volume of the solid formed by revolving \\(y=\\sqrt{x}\\) about the \\(x\\)-axis on \\([0,4]\\).</p>\\[V=\\pi\\int_0^4(\\sqrt{x})^2\\,dx=\\pi\\int_0^4 x\\,dx=\\pi\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right]_0^4=\\pi\\cdot8=8\\pi.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the area between \\(y=x^2\\) and \\(y=2x\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Intersect: \\(x^2=2x\\Rightarrow x=0,2\\). Area \\(=\\int_0^2(2x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[x^2-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^2=4-\\frac{8}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
